  "id": "conduction-velocity",
  "term": "conduction velocity",
  "definition": "Conduction velocity is the speed and efficiency with which sensory nerve signals are carried along a pathway, such as from the ear to the auditory cortex. In this context, it depends on the coordinated action of neural and glial structures and processes, including axons, myelin, synapses, dendrites, and related chemical and electrical components.",
